  "rule": "Use the unchanged V49 portable core with synchronized nine-body measurements. Preserve world foot anchors, independent upright body pose, continuous body-origin recentering, remaining-three-support preparation and all finite controller limits. The prospective Godot schedule closes walking after measured cycles for all four feet and four supported stance phases, then commands 120 zero-amplitude/zero-speed stop steps. Retain all contact losses and original diagnostic evaluation separately. No acceptance claim.",
  "parameter_basis": "Use the exact V49 DLL already checked by 362 Rust tests and the 22-test MuJoCo launch gate. Keep 20 mm support margin, 0.03 m/s COM speed, 0.15 rad/s angular speed, 0.05 rad tilt, six-command preparation dwell, 240-command preparation timeout and 120-command missing-support hold. Keep 72-command amplitude ramp and all gains, joint and motor limits. The new Godot schedule permits up to 1600 walking commands, then exactly 120 zero-amplitude/zero-speed stopping commands and a final 30-command measured settled predicate.",
  "compatibility_scope": "Select the distinct V49 policy/profile/memory/receipt and strict v3 floor-plus-measured-body request only for walking_resume. Preserve all old policy outputs and original fixed-tail diagnostics. Nine-body poses and twists come from the existing synchronized sampler with its binary64 canonical orientation conversion; the new projection adds no physics reads. Fresh V20 recovery and V7 stance remain unchanged.",
